From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marco Martins <marcomartins86@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:42:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: b43: report the TX ACK status

b43 tells mac80211 in each TX status whether the frame was acked, but
does not set REPORTS_TX_ACK_STATUS. Without it, mac80211 does not take
back a frame that failed while its station dozes (see
ieee80211_tx_status_ext()), so the frames that were already in the DMA
ring when a station went to sleep are lost: holding back the frames of
dozing stations only covers those still in tx_queue.

With the flag, mac80211 buffers them again, and they go out on the
station's next wake.

ASUS WL-320gE (BCM5352, G-PHY) as an AP, with an Android phone on it
with its screen off, pinged once a second over the wire while a PC ran
TCP downloads through the AP, 90 pings per run, 9 runs each: without the
flag, 37-62 pings were lost (median 43); with it, 0-17 (median 3). The
replies come later instead: median 199 -> 267 ms, the slowest in 8.3 s.
TCP download was the same, 14.1-17.0 against 14.3-16.6 Mbit/s.

Signed-off-by: Marco Martins <marcomartins86@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
index f3b4dc4..bfe94b8 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
@@ -6881,6 +6881,7 @@ static struct b43_wl *b43_wireless_init(struct b43_bus_dev *dev)
 	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, MFP_CAPABLE);
 	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, AMPDU_AGGREGATION);
 	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, SUPPORT_FAST_XMIT);
+	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, REPORTS_TX_ACK_STATUS);
 	/* Room for the TX header in front of the frame (one DMA descriptor) */
 	if (b43_dma_txhdr_in_skb(dev))
 		hw->extra_tx_headroom = sizeof(struct b43_txhdr);
